/* --> Behavior of an Object

1. Defination ->
Behavior describes the actions or operations that an object can perform through its member functions or methods.

Behavior यह बताता है कि Object कौन-कौन से कार्य (Actions/Operations) कर सकता है। ये कार्य सामान्यतः उसके Member Functions/Methods द्वारा किए जाते हैं।

2. Defination-->
Behavior represents the actions, operations, or activities that an object can perform during the execution of a program. The behavior of an object is generally implemented through member functions or methods defined in its class. These methods can read, modify, calculate, process, or display the object's state. Thus, behavior explains what an object can do and how it can interact with other objects or components of a program.

Behavior Object द्वारा किए जाने वाले Actions, Operations या Activities को दर्शाता है। Object का Behavior सामान्यतः उसकी Class में बनाए गए Member Functions या Methods द्वारा Implement किया जाता है। ये Methods Object के Data को Read, Modify, Calculate, Process या Display कर सकते हैं। इसलिए Behavior यह बताता है कि कोई Object क्या कार्य कर सकता है और Program में किस प्रकार कार्य करता है। */

